%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: HelgenKeep_Hadvar
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I decide to head with Hadvar.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474599036452921
    - rid: 9079474599036452923
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: We make our way into Helgen Keep.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474599036452925
    - rid: 9079474618519257088
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: Was that a dragon...?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, yeah. That was Alduin.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: The World-Eater?!? I thought he was just a legend meant to scare Nord
      children...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Oh what was it that Ulfric said...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Legends don't burn down villages.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... I think that's what he said...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, you mind helping me with these bindings?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, of course.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I walk closer to Hadvar, who cuts my bindings with an iron dagger.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474618519257141
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: There you go. There should be some equipment in that chest over there.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 'One of the better reasons to choose Hadvar: you don''t have to wear
      some dead guy''s armor!'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I open up the chest, finding an iron sword and some light Imperial armor.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... how am I supposed to put this on...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Hey Hadvar, you mind giving me a hand with this armor?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: Hmm?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: You're not experienced with fighting, are you?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... not a good look in front of a Nord...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: Here-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Hadvar helps me with fastening my tunic; I could figure out the bracers
      and boots on my own.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Thanks.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I draw my newly acquired iron sword.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474618519257143
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... I honestly thought it would be heavier...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: Alright, let's get going.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I follow Hadvar into the next room, bracing myself for the upcoming fight
      with the Stormcloaks.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Upon seeing us enter, the two Stormcloak soldiers draw their weapons.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593760
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b8f3f35a1754f8643acfe8c57dd64655, type: 2}
    dialog: Imperial dogs!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Hadvar goes to confront one of them, leaving me to deal with the other...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593761
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593791
    - rid: 9079474635428593762
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I've just killed a man...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593792
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: Good work, let's see about that gate.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593795
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Ah right, the way to the next room is locked.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Friggin' unspoken tutorials...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: One of the soldiers we just killed should have the key.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I start searching through one of them-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: <Speed=1>... his eyes are still open, despite being lifeless.</Speed>
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593796
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: Hurry up prisoner, we don't have time!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593797
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... he's not wrong.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I find the key in the pocket of the soldier that Hadvar killed.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Using the key, I unlock the gate.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Jesus-!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593798
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Oh right, the ceiling caving in is scripted to happen here.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I guess I'm lucky that the game world I've found myself in seems to adhere
      to the scripting of the actual game.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: We make our way through the dining area, encountering more Stormcloaks...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593802
    - rid: 9079474635428593803
    - rid: 9079474635428593804
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593824
    - rid: 9079474635428593814
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593816
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593818
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593819
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593820
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... we arrive to the torture room.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593823
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: I wish we didn't need these...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593833
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... I wish we had the time to discuss the morality of wartime decisions
      made by empires, but I would rather be anywhere else right now.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I elect to let the Imperial torturer and the Stormcloak woman duke it
      out, while I move on to the next room.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593835
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... how recent is this broken wall?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593834
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Since there's an actual room on the other side, one would assume it's
      been here for a while.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: But why leave it in such disrepair?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: As a testament to the crumbling influence of the Mede empire?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Where's Hadvar?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I turn around to see Hadvar approaching, clearly more hurt than when
      I last saw him.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593836
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ... did you help the torturer?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: ... I avenged him.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I see...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Let's just move on.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: We carry on... I think we're about halfway there...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Ah crap-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593837
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: There's like four of 'em here...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I decide to rush toward the lever bridge, if I remember right the slight
      dropoff just past it should prevent them from pursuing me further.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Two of the archers take aim at me-!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593838
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alright... made it past them...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593843
    - rid: 9079474635428593840
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I take a minute to catch my breath...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593844
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Hadvar approaches, breathing heavily.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593846
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Sorry for running, I didn't think we could take them with just the two
      of us.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Hadvar looked a bit upset with my cowardice when he first approached,
      but he seems to think about my words.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: ... I guess you're right. I had to run ahead after taking a few too many
      arrows.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: I've been resting here for a bit, and haven't been attacked yet...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So what's your call? Take a minute?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: I don't think we have the luxury of time when there's a dragon on the
      loose.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: While he's not wrong...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I'm pretty sure in the actual game you can wait around Helgen Keep without
      consequence.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: If you think that's the best idea, then let's get going.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Ah... screw my life...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593847
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Frostbite spiders...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593848
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: It's funny, when I'm playing the game I don't really think about them
      too much.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: But in person?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... gahhh...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: <Speed=20>HeebieJeebieHeebieJeebieHeebieJeebieHeebieJeebie-</Speed>
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: Are you alright? Scared of spiders?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ... s-scared is an undest-statement...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I'm pretty sure I can feel my legs actively quivering...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: (I doubt this boy'll be any help against these things...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: While I can hear Hadvar mumble that under his breath, I completely agree
      with his assessment.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ... b-b-book it...?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: Fine.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: The pair of us rush through the room, I'm happy to know that there's
      an exit right to our left.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I like to imagine my crippling fear actually helped me escape that situation.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593849
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... otherwise I'd feel really bad for not helping Hadvar more, especially
      since he's been doing way more heavy lifting for me than he ever did for my
      player characters.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474680798380210
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: Hold up. There's a bear just up ahead, see?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ... why yes. Yes there is.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: I'd rather not fight her right now, so let's just try to sneak by.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: No arguments here.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: We both crouch down, and successfully make our way past the bear.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: <font=futura>Sneak Increased to 10
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593851
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... I feel pretty sneaky right now...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Ah, open air! I didn't know how much I missed you!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474635428593850
    - rid: 9079474680798380177
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alduin flies overhead, luckily not noticing us.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: There he goes... Looks like he's gone for good this time.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Eh... give it a minute. I think we'll see him again at Kynesgrove?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... then again, Hadvar probably won't be there when Alduin shows up...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... I like how I just assumed I'll be doing the main quest, and not trying
      to get back home...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: There's no way to know if anyone else made it out alive...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: The closest town is Riverwood, my uncle's the blacksmith there. I'm sure
      he'd help you out.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 507b69390860cfe4ba479b15a3c06ec2, type: 2}
    dialog: It'd probably be best if we split up. Good luck.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Hadvar leaves, heading down the road to Riverwood.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079474680798380211
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Doesn't he say something about not being able to make it out alive without
      my help in the original game?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Dang.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: My stomach growls.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Ah yes, I <i>have</i> been working up a sweat without having had breakfast...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I take a seat on a nearby rock to rest my feet before starting my journey
      to Riverwood.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Heh, Sayori would probably scold me for skipping breakfast-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: OH GOD THE FESTIVAL-!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... wait, why am I in Skyrim, anyway?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: The pain I've felt so far has been pretty real, so I don't think this
      is all a dream...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I might be dead, but I really doubt I died peacefully in my sleep.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Assuming I didn't get murdered...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Hm.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: After a few minutes of resting, I get on my feet and start heading to
      Riverwood.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
  playerChoices:
  - choiceText: 
    resultingSequence: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd30022cf9b9f5f4b9c58c9932d73df9, type: 2}
